netglance is a LAN host discovery and inventory daemon. It scans the
configured CIDRs over ARP, keeps a SQLite history of every device, and
ships a mobile-friendly web UI on a dedicated port (default 8473).

This plugin integrates the netglance daemon (installed by the netglance
package) into OPNsense: a Services > Netglance tab to enable/disable the
service, pick listen port and bind address, select scan interfaces, and
declare the networks (CIDR + optional VLAN) to inventory. The web UI
itself remains accessible directly on the configured port and is
reachable from any device on the LAN, including mobile.
